   b. If the middle element is greater than or equal to the target value, update `right` to `mid - 1`.
   c. Otherwise, update `left` to `mid + 1`.
3. After the while loop, check if `left` is less than `n` and the element at index `left` is greater than or equal to the target value. If true, return `left`.
4. If the above condition is not satisfied, return -1 to indicate that there is no element in the array that is greater than or equal to the target value.

